REGEDIT4

; The system's own programs draw at the scale of the system, as in Windows
; 11, instead of being stretched like a bitmap: the picture viewer and the
; "Open with" dialog (rundll32), the Control Panel's applets, Notepad,
; Registry Editor, Paint... Image File Execution Options, which Wine's user32
; reads before a program's manifest (dpiAwareness: 1 = the system's DPI,
; 2 = each monitor's). Programs of others keep what their manifests say, as
; Windows does with them.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\Software\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\Image File Execution Options\rundll32.exe]
"dpiAwareness"=dword:00000001

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\Software\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\Image File Execution Options\control.exe]
"dpiAwareness"=dword:00000001

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\Software\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\Image File Execution Options\regedit.exe]
"dpiAwareness"=dword:00000001

